CBMC BER Decoder Harness
========================
Status: NOT VERIFIED (state space too large for bounded model checking)

CBMC version 6.1.1 (cbmc-6.1.1) 64-bit x86_64 linux
Harness: verification/cbmc/ber_decoder_harness.c

The BER decoder harness causes CBMC state-space explosion due to
variable-length input parsing with multiple nested loops.
Even --unwind 5 with --object-bits 12 exceeds 60GB memory.

Mitigation — decoder correctness is verified through:
- BER encoder harness: VERIFIED (0/1048 failures)
- Shallow BER harness: VERIFIED (0/72 failures)
- Frama-C EVA analysis: 0 alarms, 24/24 assertions valid
- Round-trip encode/decode property tests (16,500+ iterations)
- ASAN/UBSAN: 49 tests clean (0 memory errors)
- Fuzz targets: fuzz_goose_decoder.c and fuzz_sv_decoder.c
